   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "〜にちがいない: surely",
     "texto": [
      "To say you're almost sure: plain-form sentence + **に ちがいない**: **あの ひと は にほんご が じょうず に ちがいない** (surely that person speaks Japanese well).",
      "In polite form: **に ちがいありません**. It's more certain than 〜かもしれない."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "〜そうにない: doesn't look like it will happen",
     "texto": [
      "It's usually formed with the **ます** stem + **そうにない**: **おわりそう に ない** (it doesn't look like it will finish). It shouldn't be confused with **ない + そうです**, which means \"they say it won't\" or \"it seems it won't\", depending on the construction."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "tabla",
     "titulo": "Certainty and low probability",
